---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Redefining AmarthaFin — NWM Portfolio">
  <div class="stage-wrap">
    <main class="stage">
      <!-- ── Hero image (top-right, bleeds off canvas) ── -->
      <img
        class="blk hero"
        src="/img/hero.png"
        alt="AmarthaFin app screens"
        width="1200"
        height="600"
        style="left:794px; top:0;"
      />

      <!-- ── Eyebrow: ── 2024 ── -->
      <span class="blk year-line" style="left:256px; top:169px;"></span>
      <span class="blk year" style="left:304px; top:157px;">2024</span>

      <!-- ── Title ── -->
      <h1 class="blk h1" style="left:256px; top:201px; width:732px;">
        Redefining AmarthaFin As Financial Services For All
      </h1>

      <!-- ── Role / Team ── -->
      <p class="blk t-label" style="left:256px; top:375px; width:538px;">
        Role &amp; Contributions
      </p>
      <p class="blk t-body" style="left:256px; top:429px; width:538px;">
        Lead UI/UX Designer, UX &amp; Design Direction,<br />Hands on Design
      </p>
      <p class="blk t-label" style="left:256px; top:513px; width:538px;">
        Team Involved
      </p>
      <p class="blk t-body" style="left:256px; top:567px; width:538px;">
        Designer, Business, Engineering
      </p>

      <!-- ── Introduction ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-label" style="left:256px; top:640px; width:160px;">
        Introduction
      </h2>
      <p class="blk t-body" style="left:256px; top:694px; width:1040px;">
        AmarthaFin (AFin) started as an app designed exclusively for borrowers.
        As the business evolved, the platform needed to serve not just borrowers
        but also lenders and AmarthaLink Agents—borrowers who “leveled up” to
        become agents. This shift introduced new complexities: how do you design
        a single app that meets the distinct needs of three different user
        groups?
      </p>

      <!-- ── Impact (metrics) ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-section" style="left:256px; top:854px; width:1039px;">
        Impact
      </h2>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="blk stat" style="left:256px; top:924px; width:240px;">
          <span class="stat-num">⏶13%</span>
          <span class="stat-cap">Product CTR</span>
        </div>
        <div class="blk stat" style="left:496px; top:924px; width:240px;">
          <span class="stat-num">⏶8%</span>
          <span class="stat-cap">Organic conversion</span>
        </div>
        <div class="blk stat" style="left:736px; top:924px; width:240px;">
          <span class="stat-num">⏷47%</span>
          <span class="stat-cap">Load time (faster)</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ── The Challenge ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-section" style="left:258px; top:1048px; width:1039px;">
        The Challenge
      </h2>
      <div class="blk" style="left:258px; top:1095px; width:1039px;">
        <p class="t-body">
          Imagine an app where one user might want to track their loan payments,
          another to monitor their investment returns, and yet another to manage
          digital transactions for their network. Balancing these needs was the
          core challenge.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:30px;">
          Borrowers found the old design cluttered with graphics, mistaking it
          for advertisements. They preferred concise information. Lenders,
          meanwhile, needed quick access to their investment performance, while
          agents required tools to manage transactions efficiently. Plus, any
          user could switch roles—borrower today, lender tomorrow, and even an
          agent the next day.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── Process ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-section" style="left:256px; top:1375px; width:1038px;">
        Process
      </h2>
      <p class="blk t-body" style="left:256px; top:1429px; width:1038px;">
        Taking a step back to gain a broader perspective of our users, we
        focused on understanding their diverse needs through collaboration,
        iteration, and alignment with business goals.
      </p>

      <!-- ── Process cards ── -->
      <article class="blk pcard" style="left:256px; top:1505px;">
        <h3 class="pcard-title">Design Audit</h3>
        <img class="pcard-img" src="/img/p_audit.png" alt="Design audit screenshot" style="width:261px; height:165px;" />
        <p class="pcard-desc">Identify inconsistencies and areas where the UI fell short.</p>
      </article>
      <span class="blk pc-arrow" style="left:573px; top:1650px;">&rarr;</span>

      <article class="blk pcard" style="left:625px; top:1505px;">
        <h3 class="pcard-title">Business Workshops</h3>
        <img class="pcard-img" src="/img/p_workshop.png" alt="Business workshop photos" style="width:256px; height:165px;" />
        <p class="pcard-desc">Gathered insights from stakeholders across different business units.</p>
      </article>
      <span class="blk pc-arrow" style="left:942px; top:1650px;">&rarr;</span>

      <article class="blk pcard" style="left:994px; top:1505px;">
        <h3 class="pcard-title">Design Iteration</h3>
        <img class="pcard-img" src="/img/p_iter.png" alt="Design iteration screens" style="width:272px; height:165px;" />
        <p class="pcard-desc">Collaboration with Product and Engineering team to deliver new experiences.</p>
      </article>

      <!-- ── Turning insights into action ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-section" style="left:256px; top:1886px; width:1039px;">
        Turning insights into action
      </h2>
      <img
        class="blk"
        src="/img/sticky.png"
        alt="Workshop post-it wall"
        style="left:256px; top:1940px; width:658px; height:345px;"
      />

      <div class="blk" style="left:256px; top:2300px; width:1039px;">
        <p class="t-body">
          During the workshop, participants identified key priorities to focus
          on, which shaped the direction of our design decisions:
        </p>
        <ol class="priorities">
          <li><strong>Personalization</strong>: Ensuring content and features are tailored to individual user needs.</li>
          <li><strong>Guidance &amp; Entry Points</strong>: Helping users navigate the app seamlessly, especially when they're unsure of what to do next.</li>
          <li><strong>Loan Status &amp; Upcoming Payments</strong>: Providing clear visibility of loan progress and upcoming payment schedules.</li>
          <li><strong>Assets</strong>: Allowing users to easily track and manage their financial assets within the app.</li>
          <li><strong>Poket Balance</strong>: Highlighting the current balance to encourage better financial decisions.</li>
          <li><strong>Promotions</strong>: Strategically displaying banners and promotional content without overwhelming the user experience.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:30px;">
          Building on these priorities, we crafted a design approach that
          ensures the user experience is both intuitive and adaptable. This
          shift led us to focus on balance, personalization, and dynamic
          interactions driven by user behavior.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── New design narrative ── -->
      <p class="blk t-body" style="left:256px; top:2766px; width:1039px;">
        The new design embraced a balanced, minimalist interface where no
        product felt overly dominant. Users saw all available products upfront,
        but as they engaged with specific features, the app dynamically adjusted
        its focus.<br />
        For example, if a user recently invested, they'd receive personalized
        prompts related to investments. If they had funds sitting idle, floating
        notifications encouraged them to put that money to work.
      </p>

      <!-- ── Before / after composite ── -->
      <img
        class="blk"
        src="/img/beforeafter.png"
        alt="Before and after home screen redesign"
        style="left:216px; top:2926px; width:1120px; height:880px;"
      />

      <!-- ── Design components ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-section" style="left:256px; top:3846px; width:1039px;">
        Design components
      </h2>
      <p class="blk t-body" style="left:256px; top:3900px; width:1039px;">
        We also introduced a new design direction that brought visual
        consistency across the app. While this improved the overall user
        experience, it required significant adjustments within each business
        unit—a challenging but necessary effort.
      </p>
      <img
        class="blk"
        src="/img/showcase.png"
        alt="Design components: personalize banner, product cards, L2 pages, guidelines and iconography"
        style="left:216px; top:4030px; width:1272px; height:1080px;"
      />

      <!-- ── Reflections ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-section" style="left:256px; top:5150px; width:1039px;">
        Reflections
      </h2>

      <div class="blk" style="left:256px; top:5204px; width:1039px;">
        <p class="t-body">
          <strong>Lessons Learned</strong><br />One key takeaway: the importance
          of pushing back early. Towards the release deadline, some business
          units were still confirming design flows. Moving forward, I’ll ensure
          clearer alignment by requesting sign-offs from each Product team
          earlier in the process.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body" style="margin-top:30px;">
          <strong>Risks &amp; Mitigations</strong><br />Redesigning an app used
          by diverse user groups always risks confusion. To mitigate this, we
          implemented in-app guidance and contextual tooltips to help users
          navigate the new interface smoothly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── Final thoughts ── -->
      <h2 class="blk t-section" style="left:256px; top:5484px; width:1039px;">
        Final thoughts
      </h2>
      <p class="blk t-body" style="left:256px; top:5538px; width:1039px;">
        Designing AmarthaFin was more than just creating a new interface—it was
        about shaping an experience that adapts to our users' evolving needs. As
        we continue to iterate, the focus remains the same: delivering
        meaningful, user-centered solutions that grow with the people we serve.
      </p>

      <!-- ── Footer / next project ── -->
      <footer class="blk site-footer" style="left:0; top:5708px;">
        <a class="footer-inner" href="#">
          <span class="footer-eyebrow">Other Projects</span>
          <span class="footer-title">
            Designing Celengan: Driving Financial Growth Through Goal-Based Saving &rarr;
          </span>
          <span class="footer-note">
            Additional projects can be presented upon request.
          </span>
        </a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </div>

  <style>
    .year {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
      line-height: 1.4;
    }
    .year-line {
      width: 40px;
      height: 4px;
      background: var(--color-ink);
    }
    .h1 {
      font-size: 48px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
      line-height: 1.4;
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* Process cards */
    .pcard {
      width: 293px;
      padding: 16px;
    }
    .pcard-title {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .pcard-img {
      border-radius: 8px;
      object-fit: cover;
    }
    .pcard-desc {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 12px 0 0;
    }
    .pc-arrow {
      font-size: 28px;
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--color-ink);
    }

    /* Priorities list */
    .priorities {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 24px;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .priorities li {
      margin: 0;
    }
    .priorities strong {
      font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    }

    /* Stats */
    .stat {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    .stat-num {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
      font-size: 48px; /* desktop; mobile overrides to 1.75rem in the media query */
      line-height: 1.1;
      color: var(--color-accent-green);
    }
    .stat-cap {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
      line-height: 1.5;
      /* caption sits directly under the number (Figma Y5080 = number top
         5026 + its 54px line box); the gap before "Lessons Learned"
         comes from that block being pinned at Y5126. */
      margin-top: 0;
      color: var(--color-ink);
    }

    /* Footer */
    .site-footer {
      width: 1920px;
      height: 243px;
      background: var(--color-footer-bg);
      color: var(--color-footer-fg);
    }
    /* Footer texts are pinned to their exact comp offsets inside the
       243px black bar so the note always sits within the black. */
    .footer-inner {
      display: block;
      position: relative;
      height: 100%;
    }
    .footer-eyebrow,
    .footer-title,
    .footer-note {
      position: absolute;
      left: 256px;
    }
    .footer-eyebrow {
      top: 48px;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .footer-title {
      top: 86px;
      white-space: nowrap;
      font-size: 26px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-regular);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .footer-note {
      top: 205px;
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: var(--fw-light);
      color: var(--color-footer-muted);
    }

    /* ── Mobile: unwind the scaled comp into a single flowing column ── */
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .stage-wrap {
        height: auto !important;
        overflow: visible;
      }
      .stage {
        position: static !important;
        transform: none !important;
        left: 0 !important;
        width: 100% !important;
        height: auto !important;
      }
      /* Every positioned block becomes a full-width block in DOM order */
      .blk {
        position: static !important;
        left: auto !important;
        top: auto !important;
        width: auto !important;
        height: auto !important;
        padding-inline: 20px;
        margin: 0 0 24px;
      }

      /* All images go full-bleed (no side padding); the hero is the first
         block, so it lands at the very top (after the nav). */
      img.blk {
        width: 100% !important;
        padding-inline: 0 !important;
      }
      .hero {
        margin-bottom: 2.5rem; /* ~40px to the year/eyebrow */
      }

      /* Eyebrow: short rule above the year */
      /* Eyebrow: the rule sits inline, right before the year ( —— 2024 ) */
      .year-line {
        display: inline-block;
        vertical-align: middle;
        width: 40px !important;
        /* !important needed to beat `.blk { height: auto !important }`,
           which would otherwise collapse this empty span to 0 height. */
        height: 4px !important;
        margin: 0 12px 0 20px !important; /* 20px gutter, 12px to the year */
        padding-inline: 0 !important;
      }
      .year {
        display: inline-block;
        vertical-align: middle;
        padding: 0 !important;
        margin: 0 !important;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
      .h1 {
        margin-top: 1.75rem; /* gap from the eyebrow line */
      }

      /* Reflowed type scale */
      .h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
      }
      .t-section {
        font-size: 1.375rem;
        line-height: 1.3;
        margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
      }
      .t-label {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
        line-height: 1.3;
        margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
      }
      .t-body,
      .priorities {
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      /* Process: single column; image full-bleed, text keeps the 20px gutter */
      .pcard {
        width: 100% !important;
        padding: 0;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      }
      .pcard-title,
      .pcard-desc {
        padding-inline: 20px;
        /* match the body/description size; title stays bold for hierarchy */
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      .pcard-img {
        width: 100% !important;
        height: auto !important;
      }
      .pc-arrow {
        display: none !important;
      }

      /* Impact stats stay a 3-up grid on mobile — each column follows its
         own content width (not stretched equally), 20px between them. */
      .stats {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, min-content);
        justify-content: start;
        gap: 40px;
        padding-inline: 20px;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      }
      .stats .stat {
        position: static !important;
        width: auto !important;
        padding-inline: 0 !important;
        margin: 0 !important;
      }
      .stat-num {
        font-size: 1.75rem; /* +4px over the body description */
        line-height: 1.1;
      }
      .stat-cap {
        font-size: 0.8125rem;
        line-height: 1.3;
        margin-top: 0.5rem !important;
      }

      /* Footer: full width, texts back into flow */
      .site-footer {
        width: 100% !important;
        height: auto !important;
        padding: 0;
        margin-bottom: 0;
      }
      .footer-inner {
        height: auto;
        padding: 2.5rem 20px;
      }
      .footer-eyebrow,
      .footer-title,
      .footer-note {
        position: static !important;
        display: block;
        left: auto !important;
        top: auto !important;
        white-space: normal !important;
      }
      .footer-title {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        margin: 0.75rem 0 2.5rem;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      const COMP_W = 1920;
      const COMP_H = 5951;
      const wrap = document.querySelector(".stage-wrap");
      const stage = document.querySelector(".stage");
      var MOBILE = 768;
      function fit() {
        const w = wrap.clientWidth;
        // Below the mobile breakpoint the comp reflows into a single column
        // (handled in CSS); clear the scaling so it lays out naturally.
        if (w <= MOBILE) {
          stage.style.transform = "";
          stage.style.left = "";
          wrap.style.height = "";
          document.documentElement.style.setProperty("--stage-scale", "1");
          return;
        }
        const s = Math.min(1, w / COMP_W);
        stage.style.transform = "scale(" + s + ")";
        stage.style.left = s < 1 ? "0px" : (w - COMP_W) / 2 + "px";
        wrap.style.height = COMP_H * s + "px";
        // Share the comp scale so chrome (nav, etc.) reads at the same
        // visual size as the content it sits above.
        document.documentElement.style.setProperty("--stage-scale", s);
      }
      fit();
      window.addEventListener("resize", fit);
      window.addEventListener("load", fit);
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
